Package: zaro
Title: Zarr via Arrow
Version: 0.0.1.9036
Authors@R: c(person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2471-7511")), 
             person("Hugo", "Gruson", , , role = c("ctb"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4094-1476")))
Description: A low-level reader for Zarr arrays (V2 and V3, including
    sharded V3), native or virtual, from local disk, HTTP(S), S3 and GCS.
    Virtual stores read the bytes of existing NetCDF, HDF5 and GeoTIFF
    archives in place, from Kerchunk JSON and Parquet references,
    VirtualiZarr manifests and byterefs tables (SQLite, or the flat
    Parquet export read by row group). Every read is a plan of byte
    references (one row per chunk) fetched through one curl connection
    pool, then decoded in R. Zarr arrays can also be opened as lazy R
    arrays (via altarr) with CF unpacking. Arrow and GDAL (via
    gdalraster) are optional, for S3 and GCS listing and credentials and
    for some codecs.
